#{[17592186479043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479043 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "084c02e4-7974-5581-92ae-668d0f97c0f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479056 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=2 \\\\ -3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32579" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479090 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}-{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =6, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-(6)+4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88def0e2-16e4-59a7-96bb-d850c4ea1c49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479106 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=8 \\\\ -8{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=8$ and ${y}_{2}=50.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105753" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479145 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=9 \\\\ 11{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=50.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=9$ and ${y}_{2}=-49.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -49\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
